@startuml
title The `Int` binding-power ladder — derived entirely from DECLARATION ORDER

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
  BorderColor #9CA3AF
}

rectangle "LOOSEST — binds least tightly" as TOP #FEE2E2

rectangle "**mixfix** · `c ? t : e` · **Tern**\n<latex>(\ell,r) = (3,2)</latex> · RIGHT-associative\ndeclared FIRST among `Int` operators" as L_TERN #FEF3C7

rectangle "**cross-category comparisons** · operand `Int`, result `Bool`\n`==` <latex>(4,5)</latex> · `>` <latex>(6,7)</latex> · `<` <latex>(8,9)</latex>\n`<=` <latex>(10,11)</latex> · `>=` <latex>(12,13)</latex> · `!=` <latex>(14,15)</latex>" as L_CMP #EDE9FE

rectangle "**arithmetic** · all LEFT-associative\n`+` <latex>(16,17)</latex> · `-` <latex>(18,19)</latex> · `*` <latex>(20,21)</latex>\n`/` <latex>(22,23)</latex> · `%` <latex>(24,25)</latex>" as L_ARITH #DBEAFE

rectangle "**power** · `^` · **PowInt**\n<latex>(\ell,r) = (27,26)</latex> · RIGHT-associative\n<latex>\ell > r</latex> is exactly what makes it right-associative" as L_POW #DCFCE7

rectangle "**bitwise + custom** · LEFT-associative\n`bitand` <latex>(28,29)</latex> · `bitor` <latex>(30,31)</latex> · `~` <latex>(32,33)</latex>" as L_BIT #DBEAFE

rectangle "**unary prefix** · `-` (**Neg**), `bitnot` (**BitNotInt**)\noperand floor <latex>= 35 = \max_{\mathrm{infix}} + 2</latex>" as L_PRE #DCFCE7

rectangle "**postfix** · `!` · **Fact**\n<latex>\ell = 37 = \max_{\mathrm{infix}} + 4</latex>" as L_POST #DCFCE7

rectangle "**atom** · literal / variable / `( … )` group\n`atomic_child_bp(Int)` <latex>= 38 = \max_{\mathrm{bp}} + 1</latex>" as L_ATOM #E0E7FF

rectangle "TIGHTEST — binds most tightly" as BOT #FEE2E2

TOP -down-> L_TERN
L_TERN -down-> L_CMP : next declared
L_CMP -down-> L_ARITH : next declared
L_ARITH -down-> L_POW : next declared
L_POW -down-> L_BIT : next declared
L_BIT -down-> L_PRE : the +2 gap
L_PRE -down-> L_POST : the +4 gap
L_POST -down-> L_ATOM
L_ATOM -down-> BOT

note right of L_ARITH
  **THE TRAP.** `-` binds TIGHTER than `+`, and
  `/` and `%` bind TIGHTER than `*`, because
  `analyze_binding_powers` hands out
  <latex>2, 4, 6, \ldots</latex> in DECLARATION ORDER — it does
  not know that `+` and `-` are conventionally
  one level. `a * b / c` therefore reads
  `a * (b / c)`.
end note

note right of L_CMP
  Grouped by the OPERAND category, not the
  result: `EqInt : Bool` still occupies an
  `Int` slot, so declaring a comparison
  shifts every arithmetic operator declared
  after it.
end note

note right of L_BIT
  **ALSO A TRAP.** `bitand` / `bitor` bind
  TIGHTER than `+` and `*` here — the
  opposite of C. `1 + 2 bitand 3` reads
  `1 + (2 bitand 3)`.
end note

legend bottom
|= Component | = Meaning |
|<#DBEAFE> <latex>\ell</latex> (`left_bp`) | the floor an operator must CLEAR to be absorbed by the loop |
|<#DBEAFE> <latex>r</latex> (`right_bp`) | the floor the operator INSTALLS for its own right operand |
|<#DCFCE7> <latex>\ell < r</latex> | left-associative — the same operator cannot re-absorb |
|<#FEF3C7> <latex>\ell > r</latex> | right-associative — the same operator CAN re-absorb |
endlegend

@enduml
